<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thirty Years' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1618">1618</a>–<a href="/years/1648">1648</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Thirty Years War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thirty Years' War was a series of conflicts fought mainly in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from 1618 to 1648, beginning as a religious struggle within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and widening into a contest among the major European powers. It devastated large parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s intervention under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> as a great power, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> further weakened imperial authority within the Holy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war.jpg" alt="Thirty Years' War" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Friedrich Lessing · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carl_Friedrich_Lessing_-_The_Siege_(Defense_of_a_Church_Courtyard_During_the_Thirty_Years%E2%80%99_War)_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
